    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Under `# TODO: Testing`, print your model’s mean squared error.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember you can make predictions with `model.predict`.\r\n\r\n```\r\npredictions = model.predict(test_inputs)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd you can pass both your test outputs and your model’s predictions to `mean_squared_error` to find the mean squared error.\r\n\r\n```\r\nmse = mean_squared_error(test_outputs, predictions)\r\n```",
